🔁 AWS for DevOps – CI/CD Services 

If you claim hands-on experience with AWS CI/CD, you should be comfortable answering these 👇

🔹 CodeCommit
 • Why would you choose CodeCommit over GitHub/GitLab?
 • How do you manage repository access using IAM?
 • What are the limitations of CodeCommit in real projects?

🔹 CodeBuild
 • How does CodeBuild handle build environments?
 • Difference between buildspec.yml and Dockerfile?
 • How do you cache dependencies to speed up builds?
 • How do you pass secrets securely into CodeBuild?

🔹 CodePipeline
 • What happens if one stage in CodePipeline fails?
 • How do you implement manual approval stages?
 • Can CodePipeline deploy to multiple environments?
 • How do you trigger pipelines on code changes?

🔹 CodeDeploy
 • Difference between in-place and blue/green deployments?
 • How does CodeDeploy handle application rollback?
 • What hooks are available during deployment lifecycle?
 • How do you deploy to EC2 vs Lambda vs ECS?

🔹 Artifacts & Storage
 • Where are build artifacts stored in AWS CI/CD?
 • How do you manage artifact versioning?
 • What happens if the artifact bucket is deleted?

🔹 Security in CI/CD
 • How do you grant least-privilege access to pipelines?
 • How do you rotate secrets used by pipelines?
 • How do you audit CI/CD activity in AWS?
